# Code style

Prefer early-return guards over nested conditionals.

```ts
// ❌
if (typeof value === "object" && value !== null) {
  const obj = value as Record<string, unknown>;
  if (obj.someProp) return true;
}
return false;

// ✅
if (typeof value !== "object") return false;
const obj = value as Record<string, unknown>;
return Boolean(obj.someProp);
```

- `str.replaceAll(/foo/g, "bar")` — not `replace` with `/g`. Regex passed to `replaceAll` still needs the `g` flag.
- `new RegExp(String.raw`<${tag}(?:\s[^>]*)?>`, "i")` — not double-escaped `\\s`.
- `str.replaceAll('"', String.raw`\"`)` for literal backslashes in replacements.
- Avoid `/[\w]+/` → `/\w+/`; avoid `1.0` → `1`.

Comments explain why or non-obvious what. No changelog, authors, or ticket numbers.
